+++ b/a1_ws/src/cave_evaluation/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+# Running experiments from one terminal
+
+`run_experiments.sh` replaces the 14 terminals. For each configuration it starts
+roscore, Gazebo, the A1, LIO-SAM and the full pipeline. It waits until the robot
+is back at its start (or the 40-minute cap), then saves the CSV and summary,
+shuts everything down and starts the next run.
+
+## One-time setup
+
+1. Edit `config/experiment.conf`:
+   * `WORLD_CMD` – the command you used in your first terminal to open the cave
+     world (add `gui:=false` if your launch supports it; it runs faster).
+   * `LIO_SAM_LAUNCH` – only if you use your own LIO-SAM launch file.
+2. Build and make scripts executable:
+
+   ```bash
+   cd ~/a1_ws && catkin_make
+   chmod +x src/cave_evaluation/scripts/run_experiments.sh \
+            src/cave_exploration/scripts/mission_manager.py
+   ```
+
+3. Check CHAMP's speed limit. The follower now asks for up to 0.35 m/s and
+   0.9 rad/s. If `a1_config/config/gait/gait.yaml` sets
+   `max_linear_velocity_x` or `max_angular_velocity_z` lower, CHAMP will clip
+   the command; raise them or pass `-s` with a lower speed.
+
+## Running
+
+```bash
+cd ~/a1_ws/src/cave_evaluation/scripts
+./run_experiments.sh                          # LIDAR_ONLY, RGB_LIDAR, THERMAL_LIDAR, ADAPTIVE once each
+./run_experiments.sh -c ADAPTIVE              # just one configuration
+./run_experiments.sh -n 3                     # 3 repeats of every configuration
+./run_experiments.sh -c ADAPTIVE --rviz       # watch it in RViz
+./run_experiments.sh -t 600 -c ADAPTIVE       # 10-minute smoke test
+```
+
+The terminal prints one status line a minute and a result line per run. All
+node output is in `~/a1_ws/experiments/logs/<time>_<config>_<run>/`. Ctrl-C stops
+the current run cleanly; its partial CSV and summary are still written. The
+script stops any roscore or Gazebo already running, so close those first.
+
+To run a single stage by hand (with Gazebo, the A1 and LIO-SAM already up):
+
+```bash
+roslaunch cave_evaluation pipeline.launch configuration:=ADAPTIVE run_id:=run05
+```
+
+## What a run does
+
+* **Exploring** – frontier goals go to the A* planner as before.
+* **Returning** – the mission manager sends the start pose as the goal when
+  either (a) time left ≤ the reserve needed to get home (at least 4 min, more
+  when the robot is far away), or (b) no frontiers remain for 60 s.
+* **Returned / Timeout** – the robot stops and the run ends. A run that hasn't
+  got home by 40 min of simulation time is recorded as `TIMEOUT`.
+
+New CSV columns: `elapsed_s`, `robot_x`, `robot_y`, `distance_to_start`,
+`mission_phase`. The summary JSON adds `returned_to_start`,
+`final_distance_to_start_m` and `mission_events`. Goals reached on the way
+home aren't counted as exploration goals.
+
+## Changes that affect comparison with the pilot runs
+
+* Adaptive thresholds are now 0.118 / 0.130 mean brightness (was 0.15 / 0.20,
+  which the MIXED cave never reached). Use `--auto-threshold` to calibrate them
+  from the first 60 s of each run instead.
+* The mode selector is vectorised. Output is bit-identical to before, but
+  `selector_processing_ms` drops from ~400 ms to a few ms with thermal. So
+  don't compare processing time between pilot and new runs.
+* The robot is faster (0.35 m/s, was 0.18) and its goal tolerance is looser,
+  so distance and goals per minute aren't comparable with the pilot runs either.
+* The summary's `duration_s` now starts when simulation time starts, not when
+  the logger was launched.
